Lifecycle history SHALL remain permanently reconstructable.

13. Monitoring

Every active Workflow Exception SHALL be monitored for:

Compliance with approval conditions
Effective period
Risk changes
Compensating workflow completion
Operational impact
Recovery readiness

Monitoring SHALL generate Canonical Events where appropriate.

14. Recovery

Workflow recovery SHALL define:

Recovery trigger
Recovery authority
Recovery activities
Validation criteria
Completion conditions

Recovery SHALL preserve complete execution history.

15. Governance

Every Workflow Exception SHALL define:

Exception owner
Execution authority
Governance authority
Review authority
Audit requirements
Retention policy

Governance SHALL remain attached throughout the exception lifecycle.

16. Quality Requirements

Every Workflow Exception SHALL satisfy:

Explicit authorization
Complete justification
Risk transparency
Time-bounded validity
Recoverability
Traceability
Auditability
Governance compliance

Quality SHALL be continuously evaluated.

17. Conformance

A Workflow Exception implementation conforms if it:

Supports governed exception requests.
Requires explicit approval.
Records operational risk assessments.
Supports compensating workflows.
Implements monitoring.
Supports recovery.
Preserves complete exception history.
18. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted operational risk assessment.
Autonomous recovery planning.
Predictive exception detection.
Distributed execution exception management.
Digital Twin recovery workflows.
Self-healing workflow orchestration.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical workflow exception semantics.

